From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: openEuler RISC-V Package Automation <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 05:22:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bash: use the declared make_builtin_argv return type

Bash 5.2 declares make_builtin_argv() as returning char **.  Keeping the
older const char ** local declaration makes GCC reject the assignment under
the target compiler's incompatible-pointer-types diagnostics.

Patch-Source: https://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/bash.git/tree/builtins/common.h?h=bash-5.2
Patch-License: GPL-3.0-or-later
Upstream-Status: Not Submitted (package-local repair; upstream writes are forbidden)
---
 bash/testrec.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/bash/testrec.c b/bash/testrec.c
index 99c5dd7..6b70710 100644
--- a/bash/testrec.c
+++ b/bash/testrec.c
@@ -54,1 +54,1 @@
-  const char **argv;
+  char **argv;
